---
import Layout from "../Layout/Layout.astro";
import Image from "astro/components/Image.astro";
import BillMap from "../assets/BillMap.png";
import TransKnight from "../assets/TransKnight.jpg";
import InLine from "../Components/InLine.astro";
import Crowd from "../assets/Crowd.jpg";
const citations = [
    {
        Inline: "1",
        mla: "Translegislation.Com, 2026, https://translegislation.com/. Accessed 18 Apr. 2026. ‌"
    },
    {
        Inline: "2",
        mla: "“Human Knights.” Mltshp, Sept. 2025, https://mltshp.com/p/1R8X0. Accessed 18 Apr. 2026. ‌"
    },
    {
        Inline: "3",
        mla: "“Seven Themes of Catholic Social Teaching | USCCB.” USCCB.org, 2021, www.usccb.org/beliefs-and-teachings/what-we-believe/catholic-social-teaching/seven-themes-of-catholic-social-teaching. Accessed 15 Mar. 2021.\n"
    },
    {
        Inline: "4",
        mla: "“Bible Gateway Passage: Matthew 5:9-11 - New International Version.” Bible Gateway, 2019, https://www.biblegateway.com/passage/?search=Matthew%205%3A9-11&version=NIV. Accessed 18 Apr. 2026.‌"
    },
    {
        Inline: "5",
        mla: "“Unbreakable Pride - SF LGBT Center.” SF LGBT Center, 26 Nov. 2024, https://www.sfcenter.org/pride-2023/. Accessed 18 Apr. 2026.‌"
    }
]
---


<Layout  title="Theological Mandate" Citations={citations}>
    <div class="u-container flex flex-col content-center">
        <div class="flex-auto h-full w-full pt-40 z-2 text-center">
            <h1 class="text-4xl font-black py-5" data-sy-reveal="Chars">
                Theological Mandate
            </h1>
            <div class="content-center justify-center items-center flex flex-col">

                <p class="text-lg font-bold  py-4">
                    The lack of healthcare access for trans people actively hurts those people by requiring them to forgo important healthcare that is needed to live a fulfilling life. Therefore that lack of healthcare access is wrong.
                </p>
                <p class="text-lg font-medium  py-4">
                    Though the Ethical Mandate laid out exactly why every person should help trans people, there exists a subsection of people who are further called to give aid to those who need it.
                    People of faith have an additional call through the Theological Mandate. Throughout the teachings within Christianity, there is a common thread of caring for the needy. These calls to help those in need will be expanded upon in this section, as we will lay out how and why the teachings of christianity demand people of faith to help trans people.
                </p>
                <div class="py-4 w-3/4">
                    <div role="alert" class="alert alert-warning">
                        <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="h-6 w-6 shrink-0 stroke-current" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24">
                            <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M12 9v2m0 4h.01m-6.938 4h13.856c1.54 0 2.502-1.667 1.732-3L13.732 4c-.77-1.333-2.694-1.333-3.464 0L3.34 16c-.77 1.333.192 3 1.732 3z" />
                        </svg>
                        <span >
                            <div class="flex flex-col pr-2">
                                <h1 class="text-lg font-bold">A small note about this page.</h1>
                                <div class="pb-2 flex">
                                    <span class="bg-black w-8 h-0.5"/>
                                </div>
                                <p class="px-4 pb-2">
                                    It should be noted that this section is not to replace the ethical mandate,
                                    but instead to further support it through the teachings of religion. The two are separated because of the differences in beliefs between people.
                                    The teachings and writings referenced in the Ethical Mandate section can be understood and used by anyone, regardless of your religious beliefs.
                                    This merely supplements the information provided on that page.
                                </p>
                            </div>
                        </span>
                    </div>
                </div>

                <div class="py-4 w-full flex flex-col place-content-center rounded-2xl">
                    <h1 class="text-2xl font-bold">
                        The Beatitudes
                    </h1>
                    <div class="flex w-full px-15">
                        <span class="bg-black w-full h-0.5"/>
                    </div>
                    <p class="p-4">
                    The beatitudes are a guideline reminding Catholics not to be too attached to material wants like pleasure or power and seek that happiness from God instead.
                    God is telling them to cherish the parts of life considered to be painful or not immediately pleasant, and be unbothered by their worldly desires.
                    </p>

                    <div class="flex flex-row w-full place-content-center justify-center text-center">
                        <h1 class="text-2xl font-bold ">
                            "
                        </h1>
                        <div class="flex px-2">
                            <span class="bg-black h-full w-0.5"/>
                        </div>
                        <p class="h-full text-l">
                            Blessed are those who are persecuted because of righteousness,
                            for theirs is the kingdom of heaven.
                        </p>
                        <InLine Citation={citations[3]} />
                    </div>
                    <p class="py-4">
                    Those who are prosecuted because of “justice” are those being harassed and prosecuted for false reasons or for who they are.
                    The Beatitude says that God loves them especially and if they are killed, then they can find peace in the kingdom of heaven.
                    This connects to our project because it is about trans people being prosecuted for healthcare.
                    Ironically, they are being unfairly prosecuted by people who claim to be seeking justice, being specifically targeted by bills restricting access to healthcare,
                    education, legal recognition, and many other aspects of life.

                    </p>
                    <div class="flex flex-row w-full place-content-center justify-center text-center">
                        <Image src={BillMap} alt="BillMap" class="place-content-center h-1/2 object-contain" height="500"/>
                        <InLine Citation={citations[0]} />
                    </div>
                    <p class="py-2 text-sm">
                        A map of the proposed and passed anti-trans bills in 2026 alone.
                    </p>
                </div>
                <div class="py-4 w-full  flex flex-col place-content-center rounded-2xl">
                    <h1 class="text-2xl font-bold">
                        Catholic Social Teaching
                    </h1>
                    <div class="flex w-full px-15">
                        <span class="bg-black w-full h-0.5"/>
                    </div>
                    <p class="p-4">
                        Catholic Social Teaching outlines the numerous obligations and responsibilities that we owe to each other like helping the poor and advocating for just laws.
                    </p>

                    <p class="pb-4 px-4" >

                        Human rights must be preserved. Everyone has a right to live and a right to live well. One of the requirements for this is healthcare. We must therefore provide healthcare to all people, including trans people. Trans people have the rights as everyone else.
                    </p>
                    <div class="flex flex-row w-full place-content-center justify-center text-center">
                        <Image src={TransKnight} alt="TransKnight" class="place-content-center h-1/2 object-contain" height="500"/>
                        <InLine Citation={citations[1]} />
                    </div>
                    <p class="py-2 text-sm">
                        This photo demonstrates the need to fight constantly in order to remind people that trans people are people and they deserve human rights.
                    </p>
                </div>
                <div class="py-4 w-full  flex flex-col place-content-center rounded-2xl">
                    <h1 class="text-2xl font-bold">
                        Human Dignity
                    </h1>
                    <div class="flex w-full px-15">
                        <span class="bg-black w-full h-0.5"/>
                    </div>
                    <div class="flex flex-row w-full place-content-center justify-center text-center px-8 py-4">
                        <h1 class="text-2xl font-bold ">
                            "
                        </h1>
                        <div class="flex px-2">
                            <span class="bg-black h-full w-0.5"/>
                        </div>
                        <p class="h-full text-l">
                            Human life is sacred and that the dignity of the human person is the foundation of a moral vision for society.
                            Our belief in the sanctity of human life and the inherent dignity of the human person is the foundation of all the principles of our social teaching.
                            We believe that every person is precious, that people are more important than things,
                            and that the measure of every institution is whether it threatens or enhances the life and dignity of the human person.
                        </p>
                        <InLine Citation={citations[2]} />
                    </div>
                    <div class="flex flex-row w-full place-content-center justify-center text-center">
                        <Image src={Crowd} alt="A crowd of protestors" class="place-content-center h-1/2 object-contain" height="300"/>
                        <InLine Citation={citations[4]} />
                    </div>
                </div>
                <div class="border-2 rounded-2xl bg-pink-300/50 p-4 w-5/6">
                    <p class="py-4">
                        Trans people are humans and logically deserve the same dignity and well treatment as any other humans;
                        however, the prevention of the healthcare needed to live their lives fulfilling threatens the life and dignity of the trans people who are being prevented.
                        We need to keep Solidarity with these trans people to restore their dignity that is being violated.
                        Solidarity is created due to the inherent human need for reliance on others to live a life and have someone to talk to.
                        It is important literally because of physical needs that need to be met like food and shelter,
                        but also mental ones like being able to converse with others and have a connection with that. For transgender people in the South,
                        a lot of institutions and safety nets in place do not apply to the problems they face. In this way, they need to seek solidarity from others
                        like them or allies in order to get the support they need. Furthermore, solidarity is needed in order to gather enough people to make change in
                        communities so that trans people can get the support and healthcare they deserve.
                    </p>

                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</Layout>
